{
  "account": "000000000000",
  "region": "us-east-1",
  "selection": "Rows are 1-based calls[] positions, checked against sequence where present. Original captures remain the oracle; this file contains no replacement expected outputs.",
  "contracts": [
    "Both retained backends use the pinned real engine and SDK-generated requests. Native table deletion runs before store teardown.",
    "Full data/conditional old Item/ordered transaction responses and cancellation codes are compared, except diagnostic wording. Workflows with compareCapacity=true additionally compare the full ConsumedCapacity response.",
    "Create/Update compare table identity and schema; selected settled DescribeTable rows compare ACTIVE status and capacity. Engine creation timing, timestamps, warm throughput, size counters and decrease counters are not claimed. TableId, policy RevisionId and opaque PartiQL cursors bind native to local values.",
    "Unordered attribute sets, schema declarations, tags and BatchGet results are sorted. Segments marked unorderedItems compare complete hash-only-index query or full-table scan page chains as multisets, retaining per-page counts/capacity, cursor presence and last-item/key correspondence. Other Query items, lists, transaction responses and cancellation reasons retain order.",
    "IAM prerequisites use generated SDK APIs and locally issued credentials. Native principal IDs bind to their generated local IDs; delete/recreate must not inherit the old grant."
  ],
  "exclusions": [
    "data.json sequences 14-28 are contaminated by a shared-variable overwrite in the original probe; corrected operations begin at 30. Never use those failures as expectations.",
    "data.json 48-49 Scan pagination reflects unspecified native partition order; Query pagination 45-47 and full-scan count 50 are selected instead.",
    "controls.json 19-22 listing observed unrelated account tables; only isolated owned-prefix first page 18 and after-all 23 are replayed.",
    "controls.json 26 and 30 observed stale asynchronous tags, not settled post-write state. Initial tags and rejected tag mutations are selected; tag propagation timing is unknown.",
    "Native polling/credential propagation rows are not replayed as deterministic timing. Selected settled observations retain their original success/error outcome.",
    "TTL, Streams, autoscaling, audit delivery, account controls, full lifecycle/billing transitions, full capacity metering, throttling, distributed transaction contention and service propagation latency are not established by this replay.",
    "partiql.json 9 omits the redacted CreateAccessKey input; only UserName from its native AccessKey output is restored to issue a local credential. PartiQL setup uses second-seed and second-update to reproduce the state consumed by the authorization follow-up.",
    "capacity.json 34-36 Scan Limit results depend on unspecified physical partition order; scalar reads, deterministic Query pages, batch misses and transactional reads are selected instead.",
    "partiql_compound_predicates.json unordered scan rows compare complete item sets and errors, not capacity. Captured physical scan overhead remains unmodeled; query rows retain capacity comparison.",
    "partiql_ordered_partitions.json 81-83 retain numeric-key traversal and continuations, but not capacity parity: row 82 charges three native units versus two locally. Storage-partition continuation overhead remains unmodeled."
  ],
